@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.portal"

Feature: Liferay University Passport Access
	Testing the Liferay University Passport Access portlet.

Setup:
	* I get all passwords
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                                |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                                |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                               |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                             |
	* I create a support user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.user1                       |
	| Email Address | passport.user1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                             |
	| Last Name     | User1                                |
	* I create a support user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | passport.user2                      |
	| Email Address | passport.user2@pspartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Passport                            |
	| Last Name     | User2                               |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Code   | PASSPARTNER                        | |
	| Status | Active                             | |
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken" on the account "Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Manager |

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Passport - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Passport - ${staticProjectName}    |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PASSPARTNER |
	| PASSPORT    |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| PASSPARTNER |
	| PASSPORT    |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken   |
	| passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken   |
	| passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	| passport.user1@pscustomer.com.broken     |
	| passport.user2@pspartner.com.broken      |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken   |
	| passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken   |
	| passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Passport - ${staticProjectName}    |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |
	| passport.partner1@pspartner.com.broken   |
	| passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken    |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Passport - ${staticProjectName}    |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Request passport access as dxp customers
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	New passports should be able to be requested by dxp customers.

	Given I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Passport - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | PASSPORT                         | |
	| Name                       | Passport - ${staticProjectName}  | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a postal address for an account with the name "Passport - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Mailing               | False           |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 456 Fake Street |
	And I assign the team with the name "Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Passport - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign the team with the name "Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Passport - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" on the account "Passport - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" on the account "Passport - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Watcher |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Passport - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Passport - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "PASSPORT" should be part of the support site
	And the support user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportAdminTestPassword}"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to "${staticSupportAdminTestPassword}"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Guest"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Guest"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support role "Customer - DXP"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" to the support user group "customer"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportAdminTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | Passport                                 |
	| End User Last Name     | Customer1                                |
	| Company Name           | Passport - ${staticProjectName}          |
	| End User Email Address | passport.customer1@pscustomer.com.broken |
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportAdminTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | Passport                                 |
	| End User Last Name     | Customer2                                |
	| Company Name           | Passport - ${staticProjectName}          |
	| End User Email Address | passport.customer2@pscustomer.com.broken |

Scenario: Request passport access as portal customers
	New passports should be able to be requested by portal customers.

	Given I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Passport - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | PASSPORT                         | |
	| Name                       | Passport - ${staticProjectName}  | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	And I create a postal address for an account with the name "Passport - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Mailing               | False           |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
