Scenario: Request passport access as Liferay employee
	New passports should be able to be requested by Liferay Employees

	Given I assign the okta user with the email address "passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the okta group "Employees"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	When I update the support password for user with the email address "passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to "${staticSupportAdminTestPassword}"
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticSupportAdminTestPassword}"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | Passport                              |
	| End User Last Name     | Employee1                             |
	| Company Name           | Passport - ${staticProjectName}       |
	| End User Email Address | passport.employee1@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: Request multiple passport access tokens
	Mulitple passports should be able to be requested by a single user.

	Given I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Passpartner - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Passport - ${staticProjectName}"
